WEBVTT

00:15.130 --> 00:21.940
Kokoro no mori no naka kimi ni deau koto

00:15.130 --> 00:21.940
I was always dreaming of meeting you

00:16.130 --> 00:22.180
<b>Zettai Shonen</b>

00:21.940 --> 00:26.970
Itsumo yume mitetan da

00:21.940 --> 00:26.970
within my heart’s forest.

00:26.970 --> 00:33.150
Hikari no silhouette sono saki wo mezashite

00:26.970 --> 00:33.150
The silhouette of light guides the way.

00:33.150 --> 00:38.750
Itsuka ai ni furete mitai

00:33.150 --> 00:38.750
One day, I’d like to try and experience love.

00:38.750 --> 00:44.460
Kimochi to kotoba niji to mizutamari

00:38.750 --> 00:44.460
My feelings and words can be like rainbows and puddles.

00:44.460 --> 00:51.860
Omoiau yasashisa ga michibiku ashita he to

00:44.460 --> 00:51.860
The kindness we share will guide us into tomorrow.

00:51.860 --> 00:57.370
Kimi ga iru dake de tsuyoku nareru kara

00:51.860 --> 00:57.370
With only you here, I can become stronger.

00:57.370 --> 01:03.680
Sora takaku negai wo kanadeyou

00:57.370 --> 01:03.680
My wish will be granted in the heights of the sky.

01:03.680 --> 01:09.050
Nanika taisetsu ka wo miushinawanu you ni

01:03.680 --> 01:09.050
You won’t lose sight of something precious to you,

01:09.050 --> 01:18.330
Kitto motto kagayaku kara

01:09.050 --> 01:18.330
because I’m sure it’ll shine even brighter.

01:18.330 --> 01:23.760
Kimi ga iru dake de tsuyoku nareru no sa

01:18.330 --> 01:23.760
With only you here, I can become stronger.

01:23.760 --> 01:30.140
Ima dekiru koto kara hajimeyou

01:23.760 --> 01:30.140
Let’s start with what we can do right now.

01:30.140 --> 01:35.540
Mawarimichi demo ii jibun wo shinjite

01:30.140 --> 01:35.540
I don’t mind if we take a detour, 
as long as you believe in yourself.

01:35.540 --> 01:44.650
Kitto motto sono saki he to

01:35.540 --> 01:44.650
By doing that, I’m sure we can go even further.

01:58.200 --> 02:05.170
<b>A Huge, Invisible Something</b>

01:58.200 --> 02:02.800
<b>Hello, this is Miyama.</b>

02:02.800 --> 02:08.840
<b>I’m currently unavailable, but please
leave your message after the tone.</b>

02:20.580 --> 02:21.750
<b>Hello?</b>

02:21.750 --> 02:23.320
<b>Hey.</b>

02:23.320 --> 02:27.150
<b>Ayumu-kun?
Sorry, I was just in the bath.</b>

02:27.160 --> 02:29.660
<b>I figured it was something like that.</b>

02:29.660 --> 02:31.960
<b>I’m only wearing a towel right now.</b>

02:31.960 --> 02:35.460
<b>Ah... umm... have you dried your hair yet?</b>

02:35.460 --> 02:36.630
<b>It’s still soaked.</b>

02:37.200 --> 02:39.570
<b>Then I’ll call you back once you’ve dried off, okay?</b>

02:39.570 --> 02:40.970
<b>It’s fine.</b>

02:40.970 --> 02:42.300
<b>You’ll catch a cold.</b>

02:42.300 --> 02:45.810
<b>I’m right in front of the stove,
so I’m fine!</b>

02:45.810 --> 02:50.410
<b>But anyway, Minatomirai is pretty
close to where you are, right?</b>

02:50.410 --> 02:52.250
<b>Ah... yeah.</b>

02:52.250 --> 02:54.250
<b>It’s three stations down
by train from here.</b>

02:54.250 --> 02:57.320
<b>But the distance between stations
is way closer here than in Tana...</b>

02:57.320 --> 03:00.390
<b>...so it’s probably a lot closer than you’re thinking.</b>

03:00.390 --> 03:03.260
<b>Are you implying that Tana is in the countryside?</b>

03:03.260 --> 03:05.330
<b>I don’t have to imply it.
It’s a fact.</b>

03:05.330 --> 03:07.800
<b>You really are relentless.</b>

03:07.800 --> 03:09.930
<b>So is something going on in Minatomirai?</b>

03:09.930 --> 03:13.730
<b>Until recently, Mika-nee was staying at one of
her company’s branch stores in Futamatagawa...</b>

03:14.200 --> 03:15.840
<b>Futamatagawa?</b>

03:15.840 --> 03:18.640
<b>Futamatagawa in the Asahi District of Yokohama.</b>

03:18.640 --> 03:21.380
<b>Ah, near the DMV then, huh?</b>

03:21.380 --> 03:23.240
<b>You live near there,
and that’s all you know about it?</b>

03:23.250 --> 03:26.310
<b>Yokohama’s too darn big to know
everything about it, you know.</b>

03:27.520 --> 03:31.850
<b>Anyway, Mika-nee transferred to the
Minatomirai branch last month.</b>

03:31.850 --> 03:33.750
<b>So your story finally connects.</b>

03:33.760 --> 03:37.190
<b>No, I’m just getting to the good part.</b>

03:37.190 --> 03:39.960
<b>Do you remember Sukawara Akira?</b>

03:39.960 --> 03:42.300
<b>The big famous announcer from your local TV station.</b>

03:42.300 --> 03:53.270
<b>[Kannai Station]</b>

03:42.300 --> 03:43.400
<b>Right.</b>

03:43.400 --> 03:47.770
<b>Apparently, Mika-nee ran into her
by coincidence... in Minatomirai.</b>

03:47.770 --> 03:49.700
<b>So she was reporting from over there?</b>

03:49.710 --> 03:53.270
<b>Actually, it looks like she quit 39 CTV,
and is now a freelance reporter.</b>

03:54.380 --> 03:56.680
<b>Umm, then that means...</b>

03:56.680 --> 04:04.890
<b>The Summer of the Fairies</b>

03:56.680 --> 04:04.890
<b>A Journey of Touring</b>

03:56.680 --> 04:04.890
<b>Zettai
Girl</b>

03:56.680 --> 04:04.890
<b>The Murder Case of the Tap Hole</b>

03:56.680 --> 04:04.890
<b>The Pan Down Murder Cases</b>

03:56.680 --> 04:04.890
<b>An Old Summer Vacation</b>

03:57.150 --> 04:00.210
<b>Have you read Sukawara’s
“The Summer of the Fairies”?</b>

04:00.220 --> 04:01.320
<b>Pretty much, yeah.</b>

04:01.350 --> 04:04.890
<b>That book... don’t you feel like
it’s somehow incomplete?</b>

04:06.190 --> 04:07.320
<b>Kinda.</b>

04:07.320 --> 04:09.220
<b>When I heard what happened
from Mika-nee...</b>

04:09.220 --> 04:15.600
<b>...I instantly figured she became a freelance
reporter to pursue the material fairies.</b>

04:15.600 --> 04:19.530
<b>There’s been a lot of stuff going on
in Yokohama recently, right?</b>

04:19.530 --> 04:24.710
<b>You think Sukawara-san thinks the material
fairies are causing the recent problems?</b>

04:24.710 --> 04:29.810
<b>Yeah. I also think the same thing,
as does Mika-nee, apparently.</b>

04:29.810 --> 04:32.050
<b>What do you think, Ayumu-kun?</b>

04:32.050 --> 04:34.720
<b>I’ve... also considered the possibility, but...</b>

04:34.720 --> 04:36.150
<b>But?</b>

04:36.150 --> 04:38.620
<b>Honestly, I’m still not completely sure.</b>

04:39.320 --> 04:43.560
<b>Could it be because of that?</b>

04:43.560 --> 04:46.990
<b>Don’t you think what happened at the
Cat Dance the year before last...</b>

04:47.000 --> 04:49.060
<b>...was something unique and special?</b>

04:49.700 --> 04:51.870
<b>Because you want me to think
it’s unique and special...</b>

04:51.870 --> 04:56.400
<b>...you think I won’t like it if it were natural, right?</b>

04:57.410 --> 04:59.770
<b>Yeah, I guess...</b>

05:00.740 --> 05:02.340
<b>I don’t think that’s it, though...</b>

05:02.340 --> 05:04.610
<b>I see it a little differently.</b>

05:04.610 --> 05:06.680
<b>Huh? Differently?</b>

05:06.680 --> 05:07.950
<b>Yeah.</b>

05:07.950 --> 05:10.080
<b>Again, I’m not totally sure about this, but...</b>

05:10.090 --> 05:13.690
<b>...if what happened at the Cat Dance
wasn’t just some mass hallucination...</b>

05:13.690 --> 05:15.420
<b>...and really did happen...</b>

05:15.420 --> 05:16.660
<b>It did happen!</b>

05:16.660 --> 05:18.960
<b>What are you saying?</b>

05:18.960 --> 05:20.490
<b>I know.</b>

05:20.500 --> 05:24.230
<b>That’s why I think that if it could happen once...</b>

05:24.230 --> 05:27.400
<b>...it could happen again and again.</b>

05:29.200 --> 05:33.140
<b>It’s possible that something similar
happened in the past...</b>

05:33.140 --> 05:35.740
<b>...and it’s possible that it might
happen again in the future.</b>

05:35.740 --> 05:38.910
<b>Don’t you think it’s something that
couldn’t have happened only once?</b>

05:38.910 --> 05:42.320
<b>Well, maybe, but...</b>

05:43.250 --> 05:47.120
<b>That’s why, even if it may have
been unique and special to us...</b>

05:47.120 --> 05:49.590
<b>See! You really do think it was unique and special.</b>

05:49.590 --> 05:51.660
<b>Ah, yeah...</b>

05:51.660 --> 05:55.760
<b>But what I’m trying to say is that this... incident...</b>

05:55.760 --> 05:57.630
<b>No, that’s not right...</b>

05:57.630 --> 05:59.200
<b>This <i>event</i>...</b>

05:59.200 --> 06:02.370
<b>...wasn’t really as “unique and special”
as you think it was.</b>

06:02.370 --> 06:05.240
<b>Rather, it was something like seeing
a solar or lunar eclipse...</b>

06:05.240 --> 06:09.910
<b>...or a shooting star whizzing through the sky.</b>

06:13.380 --> 06:16.220
<b>I sort of understand you,
yet I sort of don’t...</b>

06:16.220 --> 06:20.150
<b>But I can definitely see that you’ve
brushed up on your logic skills.</b>

06:20.160 --> 06:22.120
<b>You’re starting to sound like Dr. Kishiro.</b>

06:22.120 --> 06:23.660
<b>No way. Are you serious?</b>

06:23.660 --> 06:24.530
<b>Yeah.</b>

06:28.200 --> 06:33.700
<b>But if you’ll notice, everything you just mentioned were astronomical phenomena.</b>

06:33.700 --> 06:35.270
<b>Those types of things
come in cycles, right?</b>

06:38.110 --> 06:39.310
<b>That’s what I’m trying to say.</b>

06:39.310 --> 06:42.080
<b>The material fairies’ materializing...</b>

06:42.080 --> 06:49.050
<b>...might have some kind of cycle or rule
that we just haven’t determined yet.</b>

06:49.050 --> 06:52.390
<b>And you’re trying to determine what it is?</b>

06:54.120 --> 06:57.460
<b>If you weren’t, wouldn’t you be less argumentative?</b>

06:59.960 --> 07:01.560
<b>Hello?</b>

07:02.660 --> 07:04.170
<b>Quite possibly.</b>

07:04.170 --> 07:05.870
<b>To you, Ayumu-kun...</b>

07:06.870 --> 07:10.370
<b>I wonder if that event still hasn’t ended for you.</b>

07:10.370 --> 07:11.840
<b>Who knows?</b>

07:11.840 --> 07:14.380
<b>Heigorou-san told me something once...</b>

07:14.940 --> 07:17.550
<b>“You became involved in something,
didn’t you? Don’t run from it.”</b>

07:17.550 --> 07:20.480
<b>“Keep going and stay involved with it to the end.”</b>

07:21.580 --> 07:24.790
<b>“If you don’t want to look back with
regrets, that’s what you should do.”</b>

07:24.790 --> 07:28.820
<b>It’s possible that I’ve gotten caught up in all of this.</b>

07:28.820 --> 07:31.860
<b>But you’re not involved with Wakkun anymore, right?</b>

07:31.860 --> 07:34.360
<b>Isn’t that enough?</b>

07:48.640 --> 07:50.240
<b>Bun-chan.</b>

07:50.250 --> 07:51.380
<b>What’s wrong?</b>

07:54.850 --> 07:55.680
<b>What is it?</b>

08:08.230 --> 08:09.630
<b>There’s nothing there...</b>

08:21.440 --> 08:22.580
<b>Bun-chan...</b>

08:24.510 --> 08:26.480
<b>What is it?
Is something wrong?</b>

08:26.480 --> 08:29.250
<b>Something’s outside...</b>

08:29.250 --> 08:31.550
<b>What is it?</b>

08:31.550 --> 08:32.450
<b>I’m going to take a look.</b>

08:32.450 --> 08:34.690
<b>Seriously?</b>

08:34.690 --> 08:36.160
<b>It’s bothering me.</b>

08:36.160 --> 08:37.430
<b>Aren’t you scared?</b>

08:37.430 --> 08:40.960
<b>Nope. I don’t feel a bad aura
or anything coming from it.</b>

08:40.960 --> 08:42.200
<b>I’ll call you back later.</b>

08:42.200 --> 08:44.400
<b>Okay. But be careful.</b>

08:44.400 --> 08:46.930
<b>Ah... I don’t think it’s
serious enough for that.</b>

08:46.940 --> 08:49.000
<b>The city can be scary, you know!</b>

08:49.000 --> 08:50.600
<b>You’ve been watching too much TV.</b>

08:50.610 --> 08:52.340
<b>Well, talk to you later.</b>

08:52.340 --> 08:54.140
<b>Yep, good night.</b>

09:15.860 --> 09:17.670
<b>Old Lady Okaka!</b>

09:29.310 --> 09:31.050
<b>Dosshiru and Shisshin, too?</b>

09:47.100 --> 09:49.800
<b>Old Lady Okaka, are you all right?</b>

