15:43.120 --> 15:46.160
<b>Bun-chan... you’re mine...</b>

15:57.370 --> 16:00.140
<b>Here you go.
It’s some okaka.</b>

16:01.910 --> 16:03.510
<b>Aren’t you going to eat it?</b>

16:03.510 --> 16:05.870
<b>Oh, you need some water, too.</b>

16:05.880 --> 16:08.880
<b>Tokimiya</b>

16:19.160 --> 16:20.090
<b>Hello?</b>

16:20.590 --> 16:24.060
<b>Are you in the middle of eating your
breaded, deep-fried oysters?</b>

16:24.060 --> 16:25.560
<b>Bingo!</b>

16:25.560 --> 16:29.930
<b>Umm... could I call you back in like a half hour or so?</b>

16:29.940 --> 16:31.640
<b>Make it an hour and a half.</b>

16:31.640 --> 16:33.400
<b>An hour and a half it is.</b>

16:34.840 --> 16:37.610
<b>Akira-san, that’s poor manners.</b>

16:37.610 --> 16:41.310
<b>When eating, you should look at the
people you’re with and talk to them.</b>

16:41.310 --> 16:42.910
<b>But I’m alone here, so...</b>

16:42.910 --> 16:45.220
<b>How rude!</b>

16:46.120 --> 16:47.690
<b>Aren’t I here?</b>

16:50.090 --> 16:50.890
<b>Yes!</b>

16:55.160 --> 16:55.860
<b>Hello?</b>

16:59.600 --> 17:00.770
<b>Yeah.</b>

17:02.070 --> 17:05.740
<b>I can see where Makki
is coming from, though.</b>

17:06.610 --> 17:11.710
<b>Do you also think I shouldn’t have Bun-chan, Shigeki?</b>

17:11.710 --> 17:13.310
<b>No...</b>

17:13.780 --> 17:16.410
<b>If I were thinking on behalf of you and Bun-chan...</b>

17:16.420 --> 17:19.280
<b>...I’d definitely think that preciously
keeping Bun-chan would be best.</b>

17:19.280 --> 17:21.720
<b>On behalf of Bun-chan, too?</b>

17:21.720 --> 17:22.750
<b>Yeah.</b>

17:22.750 --> 17:28.330
<b>If you didn’t keep him all to yourself like
Makki suggested, what would you do?</b>

17:28.330 --> 17:31.500
<b>For example, would you give him to some
laboratory to be used in research?</b>

17:31.500 --> 17:35.130
<b>He’d be taken apart if I gave him to a place like that!</b>

17:35.130 --> 17:38.440
<b>Exactly. That’s why I think preciously
guarding Bun-chan is best.</b>

17:39.340 --> 17:42.110
<b>Okay... thank you.</b>

17:42.110 --> 17:43.110
<b>Yep.</b>

18:06.500 --> 18:07.970
<b>And I guess that’s the story.</b>

18:08.500 --> 18:11.840
<b>So that’s how Yokohama is right now?</b>

18:11.840 --> 18:12.440
<b>Yeah.</b>

18:12.440 --> 18:15.870
<b>If news doesn’t come on a nationwide press release...</b>

18:15.870 --> 18:18.510
<b>...it won’t be acknowledged as something
that really happened.</b>

18:18.510 --> 18:21.410
<b>And it’s the job of the local station to discover it first...</b>

18:22.250 --> 18:24.020
<b>How’s that going?</b>

18:24.020 --> 18:27.120
<b>So far, I’ve found things like traffic light failures and strange electronics behavior...</b>

18:27.120 --> 18:30.620
<b>...but I still haven’t been able
to correlate them just yet.</b>

18:30.620 --> 18:35.790
<b>And you say you’ve gotten wind of
the material fairies over there, too?</b>

18:35.790 --> 18:39.590
<b>Yeah... but in kind of a weird state...</b>

18:40.230 --> 18:41.730
<b>Let’s hear it.</b>

18:41.730 --> 18:45.970
<b>Urban legends are starting to
float around in Yokohama.</b>

18:45.970 --> 18:48.000
<b>They come in two patterns.</b>

18:48.000 --> 18:49.600
<b>Two patterns?</b>

18:49.600 --> 18:52.570
<b>Warm-colored and cold-colored
balls of light.</b>

18:53.040 --> 18:56.810
<b>The material fairies we saw were
all warm-colored, weren’t they?</b>

18:56.810 --> 18:59.050
<b>Yet there are some cold-colored ones in Yokohama?</b>

18:59.050 --> 19:02.150
<b>And... with the material fairies...</b>

19:02.150 --> 19:05.920
<b>Was it just me, or did they seem
to give off healing vibes?</b>

19:05.920 --> 19:08.760
<b>No... I also got a similar
impression from them.</b>

19:08.760 --> 19:09.890
<b>I thought so!</b>

19:09.890 --> 19:13.790
<b>Yet here, people seem to have a
much worse impression of them.</b>

19:13.800 --> 19:15.060
<b>For example?</b>

19:16.770 --> 19:19.030
<b>Like they’ve been seen swarming
around cats or something.</b>

19:19.030 --> 19:21.500
<b>Around <i>cats</i>?</b>

19:21.500 --> 19:24.610
<b>You always seem to get fierce when cats come up.</b>

19:24.610 --> 19:27.240
<b>And the image of the cold-colored ones?</b>

19:27.880 --> 19:31.050
<b>Dark lights that bring fortune to the people.</b>

19:31.050 --> 19:33.780
<b>It’s become a big chain letter with an image attached.</b>

19:33.780 --> 19:35.280
<b>You have a picture of them?</b>

19:35.280 --> 19:35.980
<b>I do.</b>

19:35.980 --> 19:37.250
<b>Could you send me a copy?</b>

19:37.250 --> 19:39.250
<b>Sure, but why?</b>

19:39.250 --> 19:44.230
<b>The fact that there’s even a picture makes
me doubt that it’s really a material fairy.</b>

19:44.230 --> 19:50.160
<b>What we couldn’t see at first suddenly became
visible on the night of the Cat Dance.</b>

19:50.700 --> 19:54.540
<b>If they’re still advancing and progressing
now in Yokohama...</b>

19:54.540 --> 19:59.140
<b>...then isn’t it possible that we’d be able to
film them now, when we couldn’t before?</b>

19:59.140 --> 20:04.110
<b>Well... I can’t really deny that anything’s possible, but...</b>

20:04.910 --> 20:09.580
<b>All I’m saying is that someone was here on that
night who might’ve seen a cold-colored light.</b>

20:10.920 --> 20:14.260
<b>It sounds like you know something I don’t.</b>

20:14.260 --> 20:16.020
<b>Do you remember?</b>

20:16.020 --> 20:20.830
<b>On that day, that evening, there was a
landslide at the erosion control dam.</b>

20:20.830 --> 20:25.030
<b>Yeah. It was determined that illegal dumping
of industrial waste was the cause.</b>

20:25.030 --> 20:26.670
<b>That’s the clincher.</b>

20:26.670 --> 20:29.970
<b>The couple arrested for dumping said at the trial...</b>

20:29.970 --> 20:34.780
<b>...that some creepy pale blue lights
were to blame for the collapse.</b>

20:36.280 --> 20:38.210
<b>Within the industrial waste
on the mountain...</b>

20:38.210 --> 20:41.220
<b>...a huge number of pale blue lights started glowing...</b>

20:41.220 --> 20:42.950
<b>...and the whole area collapsed
immediately afterwards.</b>

20:42.950 --> 20:45.090
<b>They said they wouldn’t change
that part of their story.</b>

20:45.090 --> 20:46.750
<b>What’s your source for that?</b>

20:47.260 --> 20:50.090
<b>I heard it directly from them.</b>

20:50.090 --> 20:52.230
<b>So you also pursued them, Doumaru-san...</b>

20:52.230 --> 20:55.830
<b>I wouldn’t exactly say that,
but they were still on my mind, so...</b>

20:55.830 --> 21:00.130
<b>Then could you show them the image and
confirm if it was the same light they saw?</b>

21:00.140 --> 21:03.200
<b>It really depends on the picture,
but it’s worth trying.</b>

21:04.840 --> 21:07.880
<b>So basically, there were two types to begin with...</b>

21:07.880 --> 21:09.680
<b>So it seems.</b>

21:09.680 --> 21:14.680
<b>If the warm-colored lights in Tana helped evacuate the people before the landslide...</b>

21:14.680 --> 21:19.090
<b>...and the cold-colored ones really acted
as a trigger for the collapse...</b>

21:19.090 --> 21:22.890
<b>...then it’s the complete opposite of what’s going
on in Yokohama’s urban folklore right now.</b>

21:22.890 --> 21:23.920
<b>What is it?</b>

21:24.430 --> 21:26.790
<b>I thought it was cold,
and now it’s snowing.</b>

21:26.800 --> 21:27.900
<b>It’s the first snow of the season.</b>

21:31.100 --> 21:35.440
<b>Umm... I’m glad I was able to talk with you today.</b>

21:35.440 --> 21:37.070
<b>At any rate, send me that image.</b>

21:37.610 --> 21:39.840
<b>Do you mind confirming that thing for me?</b>

21:39.840 --> 21:41.780
<b>I’ll do it when I have some time.</b>

21:41.780 --> 21:43.640
<b>Sorry for putting you through all this trouble.</b>

21:43.650 --> 21:45.050
<b>I’ll be counting on you, though.</b>

22:04.270 --> 22:05.970
<b>Old Lady Okaka...</b>

22:21.350 --> 22:22.620
<b>Pawprints...</b>

22:52.250 --> 22:59.820
Daremo shiranai kotoba de kimi he to

22:52.250 --> 22:59.820
On that nostalgic hill, I sang out to you

22:59.820 --> 23:06.530
Utaikaketa natsukashii oka de

22:59.820 --> 23:06.530
words that no one else knew.

23:09.530 --> 23:17.030
Tomare soyokaze kawaranu omoide

23:09.530 --> 23:17.030
The dying breeze and my unchanged memories

23:17.030 --> 23:23.710
Sotto misete ano koro no boku wa

23:17.030 --> 23:23.710
gently reveal to me what I was like back then.

23:23.710 --> 23:31.150
Aa yume wo aishite hitori ni natta

23:23.710 --> 23:31.150
Ah, I thought that being alone

23:31.150 --> 23:35.950
Sore de ii to omotta

23:31.150 --> 23:35.950
and cherishing my dream would be fine.

23:35.950 --> 23:44.630
Haruka na sora ni wa ima mo kimi ga iru darou

23:35.950 --> 23:44.630
I wonder if you’re still there right now in the distant sky?

23:44.630 --> 23:53.230
Yasashiku ikiru yo afureru namida koraeta

23:44.630 --> 23:53.230
Now I lead a simple life, having suppressed my overflowing tears.

23:53.230 --> 24:02.010
Mirai no melody ga shizuka ni yureru kisetsu

23:53.230 --> 24:02.010
The melody of the future is in the quietly stirring seasons.

24:02.010 --> 24:10.720
Aitai na itsu no hi ka... mattete

24:02.010 --> 24:10.720
I want to see you again, and I’m waiting for that day.

24:10.720 --> 24:19.260
Aitai ne boku wa mada humming boy

24:10.720 --> 24:19.260
I want to see you again, but I’m still a humming boy.

24:19.970 --> 24:22.940
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

24:21.140 --> 24:22.440
<b>Grandma died!</b>

24:22.440 --> 24:23.740
<b>I’m not dead!</b>

24:23.740 --> 24:26.310
<b>No, after that final scene, you’re definitely dead. There’s no doubt about it.</b>

24:26.310 --> 24:28.940
<b>I’m not dead, damn it!
I’m living right here, aren’t I?!</b>

24:28.940 --> 24:29.810
<b>It’s just... it’s just...!</b>

24:29.810 --> 24:31.180
<b>Enough! Listen.</b>

24:31.180 --> 24:33.750
<b>The world of Zettai Shonen is all imaginary.</b>

24:33.750 --> 24:35.680
<b>And this preview itself is reality.</b>

24:35.680 --> 24:36.520
<b>So listen, I’m alive!</b>

24:36.520 --> 24:39.150
<b>The preview is reality?
How do you know that?</b>

24:39.150 --> 24:39.890
<b>What?!</b>

24:39.890 --> 24:43.120
<b>Yeah! It could be that the episode is reality
and this preview is imaginary!</b>

24:43.130 --> 24:45.160
<b>Then that means you two are also imaginary.</b>

24:45.160 --> 24:46.260
<b>I’m alive.</b>

24:46.260 --> 24:47.230
<b>Me, too!</b>

24:47.230 --> 24:50.360
<b>On that note, next time:
“A Problem We Can’t Participate In.”</b>

24:50.370 --> 24:53.430
<b>What if both the episode and
the preview are imaginary?</b>

24:53.440 --> 24:54.540
<b>That’d be scary!</b>

24:54.540 --> 24:57.870
<b>If that were the case, I wouldn’t be able
to stay here happily doing the preview.</b>

24:55.000 --> 24:59.950
<b>A Problem We Can’t Participate In</b>
